 "description": "Set in a secret supernatural Seattle realm where dragons and elves hold balance, Seven-Day Goodbye follows Elara, the last pure-blooded elf healer and dragon lord Draven’s legally bound soul wife. For centuries, she selflessly offered her rare spiritual vein to strengthen his power, trusting their eternal marriage contract. But her perfect illusion shatters brutally. Draven greedily siphons her elf life force to nourish the ambitious red dragon Seraphina, bestowing their sacred couple relic on his mistress. With a hybrid dragon egg in hand, Seraphina openly defies Elara, bullying her to step down from her lawful main consort position. Heartbroken but unyielding, Elara triggers the elves’ forbidden final spell. She embraces a seven-day death countdown: she remains conscious while her body slowly petrifies, choosing silent departure over begging for love. During her final days, she endures Draven’s cold indifference, endless neglect, and Seraphina’s blatant provocation. Once Elara completely dissipates and shreds their soul contract, the blind dragon lord finally wakes up to his heinous mistakes. Tormented by insane regret, he destroys Seraphina’s schemes and wages brutal atonement. Yet the twist awaits: Elara is resurrected by the elf tribe’s collective power, but returns with zero memories of him. Now a powerful new elf leader thriving in glory, will the remorse-stricken Draven spend eternity chasing a love he can never get back?",
