 "description": "Low‑born hybrid werewolf Serena has been married to pure‑blood Duke Adrian for five years; on their wedding anniversary, she discovers that her husband is having an affair with her personal maid Vivienne, and learns that Vivienne is suffering from a fatal strain of wolfsbane poisoning. Heartbroken, Serena resolves to orchestrate an end to the marriage and leave the estate without revealing Vivienne's condition. At an auction, Vivienne publicly accuses Serena of being a carrier of the poison; Adrian, venting his spite, bids for and wins the only antidote, then destroys it in front of everyone as punishment—unaware that he himself has already been infected through his affair with Vivienne. On the spot, Serena formally presents divorce papers along with Vivienne's medical report, severing all ties with Adrian, and departs with Kael, the pure‑blood Wolf King who has been searching for her for fifteen years. Under Kael's protection, Serena awakens her Silver Wolf bloodline and masters its power. When Adrian discovers he is poisoned, he believes Vivienne's lies that Serena is the source; desperate for a cure, he scours the land for the legendary Silver Wolf, whose blood can cure all poisons, not realizing the Silver Wolf is his ex‑wife. At the Moon Festival ceremony, Serena transforms into a giant Silver Wolf and is revered by the entire pack. Adrian and Vivienne, full of regret, beg for mercy but are refused; they then conspire with the infected elder Aldric to ambush Serena and forcibly extract her blood, but they are crushed by Serena and Kael working together, leaving Adrian and his allies covered in festering wounds and near death. Can the Silver Wolf's blood purify the sacred spring and lift the plague from the entire pack? Will the centuries‑old code of bloodline discrimination be abolished? And what will Serena ultimately decide between the throne and the man she truly loves? All remains unresolved…",
