 "description": "A mountain getaway turned into everyone's worst nightmare. Emma, her boyfriend Jack, her best friend Brooke, and their group were stranded deep in the Appalachian wilderness. In her previous life, Emma was wounded during a giant spider attack—and Jack and Brooke abandoned her without a second thought. She became the creature's meal. Before she died, she saw every betrayal, every face, every truth. Then she woke up. Alive. Back at the beginning. Everything was unfolding exactly as before. Emma warned everyone—a monstrous spider, the size of a truck, was hunting in these woods. They laughed at her. Called her crazy. No one believed her. Except for Anne, the cabin owner, and her brother Ethan—because Emma had predicted the lawnmower accident before it happened. So Emma stopped pleading. She used her memories to prepare: a bunker, spider repellent, peppermint oil, cedar branches. She saved Anne and Ethan from certain death. And she watched—coldly, quietly—as Jack, Brooke, and Maddie walked step by step into the traps they had mocked her for fearing. The spider began its hunt. Taylor vanished first. Fear replaced ridicule. The survivors banded together. Emma fought alongside the brave and honest Ethan—and between life-and-death battles, something real grew between them. When it was over, Emma had rewritten her fate. The betrayers reaped what they sowed. And she walked out of those mountains with the only man who had ever believed her. ——Last time, you left me for the monster. This time, I watched you fall into the abyss—while I was already on the other side of survival.",
