 "episodes": 60,
 "cover": "https://dramadog.app/c/29362.webp",
 "description": "Maya Carter is a medical student by day and a bar worker by night. One night, she unexpectedly saves Adrian Blackwood — a man of mysterious identity — when he suffers a sudden heart attack. In the chaos, Adrian mistakenly believes Maya stole his wallet, and tries to settle things between them with a single black card. Maya never uses the card — but soon discovers she is pregnant with Adrian's child. Meanwhile, Maya's older sister Sienna is having an affair with Victor Hale, a mafia boss. To protect Sienna, the Carter family forces the pregnant Maya to take her sister's place in an arranged marriage. When Adrian learns the truth, he rushes to the wedding venue and publicly acknowledges Maya and the child she carries — saving her, and formally pulling her into the power vortex of the Blackwood family. Their relationship does not blossom into a happy ending simply because of this \"hero saves the beauty\" moment. Adrian is used to solving problems through control and violence, while Maya insists on her own education, her career, and her right to choose. She refuses to become a \"mafia wife\" who is protected, traded, and defined by others — demanding that Adrian learn to respect her boundaries before they can even speak of love or family. Adrian's half-brother Lucian seizes the opportunity to launch a succession battle. He manipulates Victor, stirs up Maya's sister, forges DNA reports, leaks medical records, and exploits the legacy of the illegal B-17 experiment project — all to use the child as leverage and seize control of the Blackwood family. As the truth surfaces, Maya discovers that Adrian's childhood heart condition, his mother's death, the suspicious fund flows in the medical foundation, and the collusion between politicians and business all point to one long-running conspiracy. In the end, Maya is no longer just a pregnant wife caught in the storm — she grows into a doctor capable of independent judgment, organizing rescue operations, and defending patient rights. Adrian also abandons his underground control, bringing the family fortune under public oversight. Together, they establish an independent cardiac maternal and child foundation, giving those who were once sacrificed to power, money, and medical corruption the right to treatment and choice.",
