 "cover": "https://dramadog.app/c/29352.webp",
 "description": "Phaea’s mother died when she was young, and her father Creon, her stepmother Callista, and her stepsister Lena had abused her for a long time. Phaea wanted to go to the river to pray for a good marriage, but Lena snatched away the bracelet that had belonged to Phaea’s mother. Phaea chased her to the river to get the bracelet back, but Lena kicked her into the river. Zeus, king of the gods, was in his palace and saw the whole scene. He rescued Phaea, and the two formed a bond. The next day, Phaea woke up and found that the person beside her was not human. She fled in panic and left one of her shoes behind. Zeus picked up the shoe, resolved to find Phaea, and sent his parents to the mortal world to bring her back. However, time flowed differently between Mount Olympus and the mortal world. By the time Cronus and Rhea descended to the mortal world, five years had passed there. They took the shoe and searched for someone who could fit it. To impersonate Phaea, Lena, at Callista’s urging, cut off her extra toes and forced her foot into the shoe. She was mistaken for the queen of heaven and taken back to Mount Olympus. Meanwhile, Phaea had been pregnant for five years without giving birth and was locked in a storage room by her father and stepmother, where she suffered endlessly. Phaea rushed out to expose Lena, but she was locked up again. On a platform ringed with fire, Lena was about to kill Phaea and the child in her womb. Phaea’s daughter, Melia, appeared with her faint divine power to protect her mother, but Lena captured her into an orb of light. Phaea was forced to jump into the raging fire, and Melia exhausted her divine power to save her mother to a seaside in the mortal world. Another six years passed in the mortal world. Phaea had lost part of her soul and become simple-minded. Melia supported her mother by digging for clams and begging. Zeus searched bitterly for his wife and daughter and finally met Melia by the sea. Their father-daughter relationship was confirmed through the Tree of Life, and he used the True Light Orb to restore Phaea’s soul. Lena was reborn as the immortal bird Phoenix and once again entangled herself with Phaea and her daughter and harmed them. Zeus sealed Lena’s divine power, retrieved the Divine Feather, and restored Melia’s divine power. Lena made a deal with a sea monster to regain her power and came to cause trouble, but she was driven back by Phaea wielding a divine sword. In the end, Lena was forever imprisoned in the dark deep sea. Zeus, holding Phaea by one hand and Melia by the other, returned with his family of three to Mount Olympus to prepare for a grand wedding.",
