 "id": 29348,
 "title": "Reborn on Christmas Eve: My Parents Turned My Life into an Experiment",
 "slug": "reborn-on-christmas-eve-my-parents-turned-my-life-into-an-experiment",
 "platform": "miraluneshort",
 "episodes": 61,
 "cover": "https://dramadog.app/c/29348.webp",
 "description": "To conduct a controlled sociological experiment in parenting, Marcus and Diana raise their twin daughters, Elena and Vivian, separately. For eighteen years, Elena is deliberately kept in poverty, forced into hard labor and scavenging, and subjected to relentless mistreatment. Her younger twin, Vivian, grows up surrounded by luxury and given access to the finest opportunities. After a tragic first life marked by poverty and exploitation, Elena is reborn into her teenage years. This time, Elena refuses to accept whatever her parents impose on her. She studies relentlessly, earns a high SAT score, and makes her first $100,000 by finding valuable secondhand books others have overlooked. She continues her education while working to support herself. Realizing they can no longer control her, her parents scheme to saddle her with the family’s enormous debts. Elena hires a lawyer to formalize and notarize the severance of her family ties, breaking free of the control they claim over her as her biological parents. Without the backing they once relied on, Marcus and Diana’s research project collapses in scandal, leaving them bankrupt. Vivian, spoiled by her privileged upbringing, squanders the family’s remaining money and gets into serious trouble. She then tries to secure a place in a wealthy family, only to face rejection repeatedly. At the wedding, the Carters force their way in and harass Elena, demanding her wealth. In front of the guests, Elena reveals the complete evidence of their eighteen-year experiment. In the years that follow, Elena builds a business, establishes an investment firm, successfully takes it public, and creates a loving family of her own. Marcus, Diana, and Vivian suffer the consequences of their actions and fall into hardship. Elena moves forward without seeking revenge. She maintains clear boundaries while offering limited humanitarian assistance in the form of basic supplies. By passing the kindness she once received on to the next generation, she finally reclaims her life and finds peace.",
