 "description": "\"The Stepson in the Wall\" Joan, 27, was trapped in an abusive marriage—beaten by her husband Roger, patching cracks in a leaking attic. Then a scarred hand reached through the wall, sliding from her ankle up beneath her skirt. It belonged to Jules—her 22-year-old stepson. From whispered touches to midnight torment, Jules dismantled every wall she had built. When Roger caught them and raised a club, Jules took him down—then tilted her chin up with the same club and said: \"Who said I came to save you?\" The truth surfaced: behind the coercion was a love he couldn't speak. He swore to destroy Roger. After Roger was hospitalized, Joan stayed by Jules's side. In that hospital room, they finally came together. She gathered evidence—recordings, wounds, medical records. Jules handed her the club and the videos he'd filmed. When Roger attacked again, Joan called the police. In court, she testified. Roger was sentenced. As they dragged him away, he hissed: \"I'll be back.\" After his imprisonment, they stopped hiding. Jules's pursuer Emily exposed them to the press. Joan fought back—built her own law career. Jules confessed. She said yes. Roger escaped. He staged a crash, threatened Joan's brother Noah. Noah woke and revealed a shocking truth. Roger cornered Joan at her firm—Jules arrived, took the blow, and Joan fought back herself. Roger got life. A year later, Joan became a domestic violence lawyer. Jules stood beside her. At their new home, she took his hand: \"This time, I chose it myself.\" ——He reached through the wall—not to save her, but to take her from the man who broke her.",
