 "description": "# *The Origin: Tang Bohu* A short historical drama set in the Ming Dynasty. Breaking away from frivolous folk anecdotes, it tells the story of Tang Bohu, who was wrongfully implicated in the imperial examination scandal. He plummeted from the height of glory as a top provincial graduate to utter ruin. With the strategic support of Qiuxiang and the companionship of his close friend Wen Zhengming, he rescued himself through painting and calligraphy amid poverty and public condemnation. Later he became entangled in Prince Ning’s treason plot and narrowly escaped death. The blazing brilliance of a prodigy and the steadfast perseverance of an ordinary soul mirror one another, unfolding a tale of accepting brokenness and rebuilding oneself amid adversity. ## Character Profiles **Tang Bohu (Tang Yin):** A peerlessly gifted artist brought to disgrace by a false conviction. Arrogant yet sensitive, he sinks into despair before weaving half a lifetime of suffering into his brushwork — a genius whose brilliance burned bright but brief. **Qiuxiang:** Born a maid, clear‑headed and resolute. Tang Bohu’s manager and guardian. She manages his livelihood and artistic affairs, shielding him through crises. After his death, she preserves and passes down his works and story. **Wen Zhengming:** Tang Bohu’s dearest friend. Less naturally talented but unwaveringly diligent. He repeatedly fails the civil service examinations yet keeps practicing, mastering regular script over decades. He embodies slow, steady growth, standing as a foil and mirror to Tang Bohu.",
