 "cover": "https://dramadog.app/c/25338.webp",
 "description": "Eight years ago, Avery Bennett, a poor young girl, was helped in the rain by Grace Whitmore, a wealthy heiress, and from then on regarded her as the most special person in her life. Eight years later, Avery has become an independent jewelry designer. Though she lives in financial hardship and has long been exploited by her stepmother, she has never given up her dream of jewelry. She handmade a lily of the valley necklace and prepared to confess her long-hidden feelings to Grace. However, at the Whitmore family jewelry preview, the confession gift box was accidentally placed on the gift tray of Camille Laurent, heir to the Laurent family. Avery’s love letter was read aloud in public by a socialite, and everyone mistakenly believed that she was secretly in love with Camille. Although Camille publicly declared that she only likes men, she stepped in to help Avery out of the embarrassment. Later, the two had another misunderstanding due to an accident in the dressing room, and Camille became convinced that Avery was deliberately trying to get close to her. Fate, however, made them work partners. Camille was facing an important assessment for her family’s jewelry project, and Avery’s exquisite restoration craftsmanship happened to be able to help her complete the work. Forced to spend time together day and night, Camille gradually discovered Avery’s talent and kindness, and Avery also saw the loneliness behind this proud heiress’s strong exterior. Through repeated physical contact and mutual defense, Camille began to develop an inexplicable possessiveness toward Avery. When Camille discovered that the person Avery truly liked was Grace, jealousy made her lose her reason. She impulsively kissed Avery, then publicly humiliated her in order to deny her same-sex feelings, completely hurting Avery. After separation and reflection, Camille began to learn to respect Avery’s choices. The two rebuilt trust and gradually moved from work partners to truly loving lovers. Meanwhile, Grace discovered that Avery, who had once admired her, had fallen in love with Camille. Her gentle facade began to crumble, and she gradually used past favors, career resources, and the secrets between them to create distance. As an old case in the jewelry industry was reopened, Grace’s involvement in project manipulation and accident liability gradually surfaced. Camille was injured in an accident at the jewelry exhibition, and their relationship suffered another heavy blow because of the truth behind the confession eight years earlier. Avery finally saw through Grace’s desire for control and was no longer bound by the debts of the past. Together with Camille, she collected evidence, completed the re-evaluation of the jewelry exhibition, helped formerly victimized designers restore their reputations, and fought for the rightful rights of her father’s old workshop. Grace’s schemes were gradually exposed, and the relevant responsibilities were pursued. Three years later, Avery has established her own independent jewelry business and is committed to helping more ordinary people learn jewelry craftsmanship. Camille has also grown into a designer capable of independently bearing responsibility for both her career and love. The two, who once met because of a misdelivered confession letter, are finally no longer bound by status, wealth, or an old secret crush, and together welcome the happiness that belongs to them.",
