 "description": "Lexi, the daughter of a wealthy family, is kidnapped and trafficked to the docks of Miami—a territory controlled by a criminal syndicate. She falls into the clutches of a brutal thug named Harlan, enduring imprisonment and abuse. During a violent clash between rival gangs, Lexi secretly sabotages Harlan’s weapon, hoping for his downfall—a move that narrowly allows him to survive. Meanwhile, undercover agent Cole Rodriguez has infiltrated the gang to gather evidence against their leader, Royce. In the midst of a crisis, a drugged and disoriented Lexi stumbles into Cole’s room, where he provides her with shelter. Though everyone believes Lexi is mute, she is actually feigning the condition as a survival tactic. Cole gives her a whistle to signal for help and repeatedly rescues her from the cruelty of Harlan, Megan, and others; as they spend time together, the two begin to develop feelings for each other. Lexi manages to memorize a phone number and asks Cole to contact her father—Daniel, a wealthy tycoon in New York. Cole takes the risk of making the call, which arouses the suspicions of the gang leader, Royce; however, Cole manages to evade detection through his masterful use of deception. Lorraine, Harlan’s lover, grows jealous of Lexi. When Daniel falls into a coma and is hospitalized, Lorraine poses as his biological daughter, plotting to seize the vast fortune of the Blair family. Lexi sneaks into the hospital disguised as a nurse and uncovers the scheme. Incited by Lorraine, Harlan infiltrates the hospital room to poison Daniel, but Lexi cleverly swaps the poison and scares him off. Lexi seizes the chance to take revenge on Harlan. Meanwhile, upon regaining consciousness, Daniel—determined to protect his daughter—decides to play along, pretending to accept the imposter Lorraine as his own child while coordinating with Lexi. Royce eventually discovers that Cole is an undercover agent and orchestrates a plan to drug him and hand him over to Lorraine. Cole, however, turns the situation to his advantage and manages to rendezvous with Lexi. When the time was right, federal agents closed in; cornered, Royce took Lorraine hostage. Lexi skillfully escalated the tension, helping Cole subdue Royce, which led to the public exposure of Lorraine’s elaborate identity fraud. In the aftermath, Cole—mindful of the dangers surrounding his own life and the vast disparity between his and Lexi’s worlds—deliberately kept his distance. Unwilling to part ways, Lexi managed to cross paths with him again by taking on a witness protection assignment. Ultimately, having weathered their trials, the two embraced by the seaside, finding their own happy ending together.",
 "about": "Sold to the Mob: The Boss Is Obsessed With Me is an English short drama in 60 episodes, originally released on MiraluneShort. It falls under Mafia & Gangster, Heir & Heiress, Billionaire & CEO and Hidden Identity. Viewers on MiraluneShort rate it 8.2 out of 10. Every episode is free to watch on DramaDog, with no app or sign-up.",
