 "episodes": 65,
 "cover": "https://dramadog.app/c/31412.webp",
 "description": "Isabella, the ninth princess of Valoria, grew up alongside Count Adrian — but he repeatedly hurt her by taking Viola's side. Viola, the orphan of the man who once saved Adrian's life, stole Isabella's life-saving medicine by faking her own poisoning, destroyed the wedding dress left by Isabella's late queen mother, wounded herself and framed Isabella, and even hired an assassin to shoot her with a poisoned arrow. Not only did Adrian believe every lie, he drew his sword and wounded Isabella himself, gave the only antidote to Viola, and started an affair with her. Isabella's heart died completely. She volunteered to marry Alexander, the Duke of the Northern Realm, to seal a peace alliance between their two nations, and left a letter cutting off all ties with her past. After Isabella left, Adrian accidentally overheard Viola bragging about her schemes. Once he verified the truth, he volunteered to endure a public flogging, then rode north wounded to chase after her. Meanwhile, Isabella had won Alexander's respect through her kindness and sense of responsibility. He revealed his true identity to test her, apologized for his earlier coldness, stood firmly by her when his childhood friend Elena tried to frame Isabella, drove the troublemaker away, cared for her carefully, and remade the wedding dress her mother had left behind — until Isabella finally opened her heart again. On the wedding day, Adrian burst in begging to rekindle their old relationship, but Isabella refused. Viola, who had escaped from prison, charged at Isabella with a dagger. Adrian took the blade for her and was gravely wounded. Isabella was grateful, but she refused to restart what was already over. In the end, Viola was dragged away to stand trial, Adrian accepted reality and left in silence, and Isabella chose Alexander firmly. The wedding was completed, and a new life began.",
