 "description": "Vera Castro, the mistress of San Diego's Castro Ocean Group, had just given birth to her daughter and been discharged from the hospital when, at the group's board cocktail party, she discovered that her husband Daryl had brought along his young assistant Selena—who closely resembled his first love. Selena even stood at Vera's exclusive speaking spot engraved with her name and delivered a toast to the assembled board members on her behalf. Vera endured and struck back, publicly making Selena take off the expedition team's life vest and cut the woven name band—but afterward, Daryl gave the custom anchor necklace symbolizing their marriage to Selena, and handed Vera the shell keychain that came free with the brand. Vera then discovered that her photo had been swapped out, her chief researcher nameplate was being used to prop up the coffee machine, and the resin memorial plaque of her daughter's handprint had been smashed. She finally saw clearly that her husband had crossed the line again and again in front of his first love's stand-in. She revoked all of Selena's access permissions, withdrew the five-billion ocean expedition fund investment, recalled three expedition fleets, and initiated CEO removal proceedings, driving the group toward bankruptcy.",
